  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "All high-transfer experimental analogues report oral bioavailability ≥20% (mostly 40–100%), including a fasting-state thalidomide measurement of 80–100%; therefore the query is predicted to have high oral bioavailability at the F≥20% threshold.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule itself.",
    "Most evidence comes from smaller, more soluble drugs; the query is a larger lipophilic anthraquinone, so solubility/efflux effects are not directly covered by the analogues."
  ],
